  "step_3": "The decision reason requires adjusting outcomes with probability less than 20% by increasing their weight by 10 percentage points. However, in this problem, all non-zero outcomes (the positive gains) have probabilities of 33% and 34%, both above 20%, so no such adjustment applies. Therefore, the condition for applying the decision reason is not met. The individual’s justification is based solely on preferring the higher monetary gain when probabilities are similar, which is a different reasoning process. There is no indication that the individual considered or applied any weighting adjustment for low-probability outcomes. Since the decision reason is not applicable to the lotteries in this problem and the individual did not mention or use any such adjustment, the decision reason was not used. Thus, the assessment is that the decision reason was not used.",
